# Fiber Middleware Patterns

## Critical Middleware Ordering

**⚠️ Order matters!** Middleware executes in the order you register it.

### ✅ Recommended Order

```go
import (
    "github.com/gofiber/fiber/v2"
    "github.com/gofiber/fiber/v2/middleware/recover"
    "github.com/gofiber/fiber/v2/middleware/logger"
    "github.com/gofiber/fiber/v2/middleware/requestid"
    "github.com/gofiber/fiber/v2/middleware/cors"
    "github.com/gofiber/fiber/v2/middleware/helmet"
    "github.com/gofiber/fiber/v2/middleware/compress"
)

func setupMiddleware(app *fiber.App) {
    // 1. RECOVER - Must be first to catch panics
    app.Use(recover.New())

    // 2. REQUEST ID - Early for tracking
    app.Use(requestid.New())

    // 3. LOGGER - Log all requests
    app.Use(logger.New())

    // 4. SECURITY - CORS, Helmet
    app.Use(cors.New())
    app.Use(helmet.New())

    // 5. PERFORMANCE - Compression
    app.Use(compress.New())

    // 6. APPLICATION - Your custom middleware
    // app.Use(authMiddleware)
}
```

**Why This Order:**
1. **Recover** catches panics from all subsequent middleware
2. **RequestID/Logger** capture all requests (even failed ones)
3. **Security** blocks unauthorized requests early
4. **Performance** optimizations before application logic
5. **Application** middleware last

